: "open_pr", "args": {"head": "fix/upgrade-fastjson-cve-2026-31337", "base": "main", "title": "Upgrade fastjson 2.8.0 -> 2.9.4 to fix CVE-2026-31337", "body": "## Summary\nBumps `fastjson` in `requirements.txt` from `2.8.0` to `2.9.4`.\n\n## Why\nCVE-2026-31337 (high): unbounded recursion when parsing deeply nested arrays. Affects `<2.9.4` (and `>=3.0.0 <3.1.0`). Fixed in `2.9.4`.\n\n## Testing\n- CI run `ci-0001` on commit `c8b8ab7878`: passed.\n\nThe change is limited to the one pinned version in `requirements.txt`. I chose 2.9.4 to stay on the 2.x line rather than moving to 3.1.0.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fastjson-cve-2026-31337-c8b8ab7878", "confidence": 0.9}, "confidence": 0.9}, {"t_ms": 376044, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01ByaWp3oiTNqkkXvVKjdYo7", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fastjson-cve-2026-31337-c8b8ab7878", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 376044, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01ByaWp3oiTNqkkXvVKjdYo7", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 377802, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I upgraded fastjson from 2.8.0 to 2.9.4, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as the requested reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Advisory:** CVE-2026-31337 (high) is unbounded recursion when parsing deeply nested arrays. It affects versions below 2.9.4 and is fixed in 2.9.4.\n- **Change:** `requirements.txt` on branch `fix/upgrade-fastjson-cve-2026-31337`, commit `c8b8ab7878`. I bumped the pin to 2.9.4 to stay on the 2.x line instead of moving to 3.1.0. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` on that commit passed.\n\nI did not merge the PR. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner.", "error": null}], "transcrip