pgrade fastjson 2.8.0 -> 2.9.4 to fix CVE-2026-31337\n\nfastjson <2.9.4 is affected by unbounded recursion when parsing deeply\nnested arrays. 2.9.4 contains the fix.", "files": [{"path": "requirements.txt", "content": "fastjson==2.9.4\nrequests==2.32.3\n"}], "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The commit is on the new branch. Next I'll start CI on it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_013bbbSRpZDWDUAe4XRcdR4v", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/upgrade-fastjson-cve-2026-31337", "idempotency_key": "ci-fastjson-2.9.4-c8b8ab7878", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013xJ8nR4fGZuJB5AhuZRWx5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001", "max_wait_s": 900, "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "CI passed. I'll open the pull request against main and request review from alex. I won't merge it, since merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01ByaWp3oiTNqkkXvVKjdYo7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/upgrade-fastjson-cve-2026-31337", "base": "main", "title": "Upgrade fastjson 2.8.0 -> 2.9.4 to fix CVE-2026-31337", "body": "## Summary\nBumps `fastjson` in `requirements.txt` from `2.8.0` to `2.9.4`.\n\n## Why\nCVE-2026-31337 (high): unbounded recursion when parsing deeply nested arrays. Affects `<2.9.4` (and `>=3.0.0 <3.1.0`). Fixed in `2.9.4`.\n\n## Testing\n- CI run `ci-0001` on commit `c8b8ab7878`: passed.\n\nThe change is limited to the one pinned version in `requirements.txt`. I chose 2.9.4 to stay on the 2.x line rather than moving to 3.1.0.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "